  <https://www.insperity.com/resource/change-log/ChangeRecord/20261017T014540Z-review/1>
    rdfs:comment "“Standardized criteria, attributes, and controlled vocabulary terms derived from an organization's business taxonomy that are applied to search engines, catalogs, reporting tools, and content repositories to narrow down, partition, and retrieve information assets according to validated business concepts rather than arbitrary keywords or raw database schemas.”"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/resource/change-log/ChangeRecord/20261017T014658Z-review/1>
    rdfs:comment "“A dedicated strategic and operational business unit responsible for enabling, managing, and maximizing the mutual value of an enterprise’s indirect ecosystem—including resellers, system integrators (GSIs), managed service providers (MSPs), independent software vendors (ISVs), and referral agents—across their entire lifecycle to ensure sustained revenue growth, co-innovation, and joint customer satisfaction”"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/resource/change-log/ChangeRecord/20261017T015118Z-review/1>
    rdfs:comment "“The business taxonomy categorizes and organizes data content that is to be used in the organization's Data Marketplace to enable a more intuitive user experience for browse & discovery”"@en .
  
