    rdfs:comment "→ “Enterprise Data & AI” (old label kept as alternative)"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/resource/change-log/ChangeRecord/20261017T015940Z-review/1>
    rdfs:comment "→ “Enterprise data & artificial intelligence” (old label kept as alternative)"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/resource/change-log/ChangeRecord/20261017T020547Z-review/1>
    rdfs:comment "“n abstract, top-level generalized entity representing any autonomous human actor (Individual / Natural Person) or legally recognized group, collective, or organization (Institution / Legal Entity) that has agency, can incur legal rights and obligations, possess assets, or enter into transactions and relationships within an enterprise ecosystem”"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/resource/change-log/ChangeRecord/20261017T020915Z-review/1>
    rdfs:comment "“n abstract, top-level generalized entity representing any autonomous human actor (Individual / Natural Person) or legally recognized group, collective, or organization (Institution / Legal Entity) that has agency, can incur legal rights and obligations, possess assets, or enter into transactions and relationships within an enterprise ecosystem.”"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/resource/change-log/ChangeRecord/20261017T021003Z-review/1>
    rdfs:comment "“The shared domain includes reference data information that is usable across content areas and describes content that is used across the organization with the same definition.”"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/resource/change-log/ChangeRecord/20261017T021100Z-review/1>
    rdfs:comment "“A concrete, instantiated business measurement modeled as an independent first-class data object—combining a quantitative calculation formula, standardized semantic definition, grain, and governance attributes—used to demonstrate, validate, or document how business performance indicators are structured and evaluated across analytical systems.”"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/resource/change-log/ChangeRecord/20261017T021538Z-review/1>
    rdfs:comment "“The business operations taxonomy categorizes and organizes information providing a comprehensive view of the organization's operational landscape”"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/resource/change-log/ChangeRecord/20261017T021956Z-review/1>
    rdfs:comment "→ “Core business operations taxonomy” (old label kept as alternative)"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/resource/change-log/ChangeRecord/20261017T022031Z-review/1>
    rdfs:comment "“The business operations taxonomy categorizes and organizes information, providing a comprehensive view of the organization's operational landscape”"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/resource/change-log/ChangeRecord/20261017T173555Z-review/1>
    rdfs:comment "“This ontology defines the core concepts of domains representing core areas of knowledge or expertise at the organization.”"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/resource/change-log/ChangeRecord/20261017T182124Z-review/1>
    rdfs:comment "“An ontology that defines the concepts and relations shared by every domain of the company, aligned to Basic Formal Ontology and anchored on the process step, so that every domain ontology extends it and every fact can be traced to the step in which it is created, used, or governed.”"@en .
  
